<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea to diversify corn imports away from U.S..</title>
<headline>Korea to diversify corn imports away from U.S..</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korean corn importers will turn increasingly to countries like China and Argentina for grain imports and trim its heavy dependence on the United States, grain traders said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;China will be the second largest exporter to South Korea this year as they have sold more than one million tonnes of corn since January,&quot; a dealer at a foreign commodity firm in Korea said.</p>
<p>Corn imports from Argentina also surged to 478,096 tonnes in 1996 from 25,797 tonnes in the previous year.  </p>
<p>In contrast, corn imports from the U.S. fell 8.8 percent to 8.061 million tonnes in 1996, an official with the Korea International Trade Association said.</p>
<p>Grain imports in 1995 reached 8.836 million tonnes, some 98 percent of Korea's grain imports for the year.</p>
<p>Corn imports from South Africa also fell to 75,995 tonnes last year against 113,243 tonnes in 1995, the official said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
